# maxxecu-07k.wv
# MaxxECU Race <-> VW 07K (CBUA/BGP 2.5L inline-5) Engine Harness (Phase 3)
#
# Same MaxxECU RACE ECU as M52 phase — zero ECU cost at swap.
# Firewall bulkhead: engine mating plug swaps (M52 out, 07K in). Cabin side mostly
# permanent — NO bulkhead additions: APS pedal wires are cabin-to-cabin (see below).
# Source: ME7.1.1 pinout — https://drive.google.com/file/d/15RPWyYPLHGEMMQZIlUgpoo77T-CxjyMP/
#         MaxxECU pinout: maxxecu.com/webhelp/wirings-maxxecu_pinout.html
#         MaxxECU e-throttle: maxxecu.com/webhelp/settings-ethrottle.html
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CRIMP TOOLS — which tool for which contact in this harness:
#
#   AS79 size-22 contacts           → Daniels AFM8 (M22520/2-01) + K42 positioner (pin) / K40 (socket)
#   VAG JMT/JPT pigtail contacts    → Engineer PA-09
#     (cam · crank · MAP · CLT · IAT · knock · EV14 injector · 07K COP)
#   MaxxECU C1/C2 Molex contacts    → Molex 63811-9200 (small) / 63811-8900 (large)
#
#   Wire stripper                   → Ideal Stripmaster 45-097 + L4994 blades, 16–26 AWG fixed-notch (do not use auto-adjusting strippers on 22 AWG TXL)
#
# Full tool-to-connector reference: e36-wiring/docs/harness-build.md § Tools
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# CABIN UNCHANGED: virtual clutch position sensor (C2 AIN 5) carries from M52 phase
#   with zero re-work. Pedal, sensor, and C2 wiring are cabin-side and engine-agnostic.
#   See maxxecu-m52.wv CLUTCH_POS_SENSOR / ECU_C2 for sensor wiring detail.
#
# KEY DIFFERENCES FROM M52 (harness rebuild required — engine mating plug swap):
#   + 5-cylinder: INJ 1-5, IGN 1-5. INJ 6 / IGN 6 cavity-plugged.
#   + DBW throttle body (07K native, ~65mm) replaces cable TPS.
#     Motor+/Motor- use MaxxECU C2 H4/H2 (MOTOR 1+/MOTOR 1-). NOT GPO3/4.
#     GPO3 → VVT solenoid. GPO4 → freed/spare.
#     Motor wires cross AS79 bulkhead via pins 22 (Motor+) and 23 (Motor-).
#     TPS1 → AS79 pin 48 (CMC G2, was M52 TPS). TPS2 → AS79 pin 56 (CMC J2/AIN2).
#   + VW cam Hall sensor (+5V type): different connector body; SAME AS79 pin 19 as M52 cam.
#   + VW crank VR 60-2: same trigger type as M52, different connector body.
#     SAME AS79 pins 16/17/18 as M52 crank. MaxxECU trigger type N-1 unchanged.
#     Only crank angle offset needs recalibrate.
#   + Bosch EV14 injectors (ID1050x x5): M50 harness ships with EV1 pigtails —
#     replace with EV14 pigtail ends at engine-side harness build.
#   + 2x Bosch flat knock sensors: route through AS79 expansion pins 43/44/45.
#   + NO VANOS solenoid. NO ICV. GPO 3 → VVT solenoid. GPO 5 freed from ICV B → reassigned to reverse light relay (MTune change only — no rewiring). GPO 4 → spare.
#   + PST-F1: same wiring, new mount (iABED M10x1.0 port) — no wiring change.
#   + WBO2 LSU 4.9: same wiring, new bung in 07K top-mount exhaust manifold.
#   + CABIN-SIDE ADDITION: BMW E46 DBW accelerator pedal installed.
#     CABIN-TO-CABIN ONLY (no bulkhead crossing): pedal (footwell) → MaxxECU C2
#     directly. APS1 → C2 E4 (AIN 6), APS2 → C2 F1 (AIN 7). +5V → CMC G1,
#     GND → CMC H1. AS79 pins 72-77 are NOT used for APS.
#     See harnesses/epedal-bmw-e46.wv.
#   + OEM ME7.1.1 engine connector reference:
#     Crank VR: ME7 pin 82  |  Cam Hall: pin 86  |  CLT: pin 93  |  MAP: pin 101
#     INJ 1-5: pins 96/97/112/88/89  |  IGN 1-5: pins 102/103/111/94/95
#     Knock: pins 106/107  |  DBW TB: pins 84(Mot+)/92(Mot-)/117(TPS1)/118(TPS2)
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TODOs (verify at engine-side harness build):
#
# DONE: VW 07K crank sensor connector body (Conn B; 60-2 VR sensor).
#       2 active signal wires + shield (3-pin housing) confirmed per BGP wiring diagram.
#       BGP source: the07k.wiki/upload/f/fd/BGP_Wiring_diagram.pdf
#       NCA in diagram = "No Connector Adapter" — sensor pigtail wires into ECM
#       harness directly; sensor body still has a 3-pin housing.
#       Location: cylinder 5 side — G28 "secured to the control housing cover"
#       (timing chain compartment cover). Source: charm.li CBTA/BGP component
#       locations, item 12. Intake vs exhaust face: unverified this session.
#       Connector family: VW 3-pin oval sensor housing (same body as cam, diff pinout)
#       — verify OE# 3B0973703G at engine before ordering pigtail.
#
# DONE: VW 07K cam Hall sensor supply confirmed +5V.
#       3-pin confirmed. Supply confirmed +5V from ECM sensor reference rail
#       (same rail as MAP/TPS) — standard Hall effect, NOT +12V.
#       BGP source: the07k.wiki/upload/f/fd/BGP_Wiring_diagram.pdf (Diagram 4)
#       Location (BGP "top front"): intake side, top of head.
#       Wire to MaxxECU: +5V sensor supply, sensor GND, signal → HOME input.
#       Connector housing: verify at engine before ordering pigtail.
#
# TODO: VW 07K CLT connector body — 2-pin confirmed (BGP Diagram 4).
#       BGP source: the07k.wiki/upload/f/fd/BGP_Wiring_diagram.pdf
#       CBUA source: the07k.wiki/upload/3/38/CBUA-wiring-diagram.pdf
#       Housing is VW-specific, NOT Bosch JPT 2-way — verify at engine.
#       Location (BGP "right rear"): cylinder 1 side + exhaust side.
#       In E36: near the radiator end of the engine, on the exhaust face.
#       Route pigtail with heat sleeving — adjacent to exhaust manifold face.
#
# TODO: VW 07K DBW throttle body connector body and motor wire polarity.
#       Confirm TPS1/TPS2 pin assignment at TB connector.
#       Verify ETh motor wire polarity at TB before wiring (swap if TB runs backwards).
#
# DONE: MaxxECU ETh1 motor assignment CONFIRMED — C2 H4 (MOTOR 1+) and C2 H2 (MOTOR 1-).
#       NOT GPO3/GPO4. MaxxECU RACE C2 has dedicated H-bridge outputs for e-throttle.
#       Source: MaxxECU RACE GEN1 C2 pinout (maxxecu.com/webhelp/wirings-maxxecu_pinout.html).
#       GPO3 → VVT solenoid (CMC D4). GPO4 → freed/spare.
#       Motor wires cross AS79 via cabin pins 22 (C2 H4) and 23 (C2 H2).
#       In MTune: Settings → E-Throttle → Motor output → Motor 1 (not GPO).
#
# DONE: Injector firing order — 07K order is 1-2-4-5-3 (confirmed).
#       Physical wiring: INJ 1 → Cyl 1, INJ 2 → Cyl 2, ... INJ 5 → Cyl 5 (sequential).
#       MaxxECU handles timing: MTune → Engine → Injectors → Firing order: 1-2-4-5-3.
#       INJ CMC channels: K1/K2/M1/M2/M3 (CMC pins 37/38/45/46/47).
#       Source: VW 07K CBUA/BGP documentation; confirmed standard VW I5 firing order.
#
# DONE: Ignition firing order — same 1-2-4-5-3 as fuel.
#       Physical wiring: IGN 1 → Coil 1, IGN 2 → Coil 2, ... IGN 5 → Coil 5 (sequential).
#       MaxxECU handles timing: MTune → Engine → Ignition → Firing order: 1-2-4-5-3.
#       IGN CMC channels: A2/A3/B2/B3/C2 (CMC pins 2/3/6/7/10). GND = L4 (CMC pin 44).
#       Source: VW 07K CBUA/BGP documentation; confirmed standard VW I5 firing order.
#
# TODO: Wire bung for WBO2 in 07K top-mount exhaust manifold (custom fab).
#       Confirm bung position upstream of turbo, min 6in from collector.
#
# DONE: EWS2 bypass not needed — 07K has no factory immobilizer in MaxxECU context.
#       07K (CBUA/BGP) ECM communicates via K-line/OBD2; no EWS immobilizer ring.
#       MaxxECU replaces the ECM entirely. No bypass loop required.
#       Body harness CAN/K-line: body modules (cluster, DME) are either deleted or
#       replaced by Gauge.S (CAN) and 8HP TCU (CAN). No OBD interference expected.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

connectors:

  # ── MaxxECU Race auxiliary connectors (IDENTICAL TO M52 — no changes) ──────

  ECU_16PIN:
    type: "MaxxECU M50 terminated harness — 16-pin aux breakout"
    subtype: "REV2. Source: maxxecu.com/webhelp/wirings-terminated_engine_harness-bmw_m50.html"
    pincount: 16
    pinlabels:
      - "+5V OUT"           # 1
      - "Sensor GND"        # 2
      - "INJ 7 (N/A)"       # 3
      - "GPO 8 / TACHO"     # 4
      - "GPO 7 / DIN 3"     # 5  — Flex fuel (if retained)
      - "GPO 6 (FAN — CAN cmd → PMU16 O3)"       # 6  — no physical relay wire; MaxxECU broadcasts over CAN1
      - "GPO 3 (VVT solenoid — via CMC D4 direct; ETh motor = C2 H4/H2, NOT GPO)"  # 7  — 07K: VVT actuator (freed from VANOS). ECU_16PIN pin 7 not used for ETh motor.
      - "GPO 2 (Fuel pump — CAN cmd → PMU16 O4)" # 8  — no physical relay wire; MaxxECU broadcasts over CAN1
      - "CAN L"             # 9
      - "CAN H"             # 10
      - "AIN 4 (MAP)"       # 11
      - "AIN 3 (PST pres)"  # 12
      - "AIN 2 (spare)"     # 13
      - "AIN 1 (PST temp)"  # 14
      - "DIN 2 (UP)"        # 15
      - "DIN 1 (DOWN)"      # 16

  ECU_12PIN:
    type: "MaxxECU M50 terminated harness — 12-pin power/chassis breakout"
    subtype: "REV2"
    pincount: 12
    pinlabels:
      - "+12V coils/injectors (pin 1)"     # 1
      - "Coil/inj relay trigger (pin 2 — N/C, PMU16 O2)"   # 2  — unconnected; PMU16 O2 supplies coil/inj rail via CAN
      - "Fuel pump relay trigger (pin 3 — N/C, PMU16 O4)" # 3  — unconnected; PMU16 O4 drives pump via CAN
      - "Chassis GND (pin 4)"              # 4
      - "Engine GND (pin 5)"              # 5
      - "Starter input / CAS (pin 6)"     # 6
      - "+12V ECU power (pin 7)"          # 7
      - "+12V ignition switched (pin 8)"  # 8
      - "Coolant fan relay trigger (pin 9 — N/C, PMU16 O3)" # 9  — unconnected; PMU16 O3 drives fan via CAN
      - "Alternator D+ (pin 10)"          # 10
      - "AC enable (pin 11)"              # 11
      - "Alternator +12V (pin 12)"        # 12

  # ── MaxxECU CMC main connector — SAME AS M52, updated GPO notes ─────────────
  # Source: maxxecu.com/webhelp/wirings-maxxecu_pinout.html
  # GPO 3 (D4/pin 16): freed from VANOS → VVT actuator (07K intake cam)
  # GPO 4 (E4/pin 20): freed from ICV A → SPARE (NOT Motor- — see C2 below)
  # GPO 5 (A1/pin 1):  freed from ICV B → reassigned to reverse light relay (Phase 3).
  #                    MTune change only: remap GPO 5 to reverse lights output. No rewiring needed.
  #                    Source: 34-ecu-harness-final.md line 23, 8hp-body-integrations.wv lines 40-41.
  # ETh Motor+/Motor-: MaxxECU C2 H4 (MOTOR 1+) and C2 H2 (MOTOR 1-). NOT GPO3/GPO4.
  #   C2 has dedicated H-bridge outputs for e-throttle.
  #   Motor+ (C2 H4) → AS79 cabin pin 22 → TB motor lead.
  #   Motor- (C2 H2) → AS79 cabin pin 23 → TB motor lead.
  # GPO 2 (C4/pin 12): fan/pump NO LONGER physical relay wires — MaxxECU broadcasts
  # GPO 6 (B1/pin 5):  fan/pump states over CAN1 → PMU16 maps to O3/O4 outputs.
  #                    12-pin relay trigger pins 2/3/9 are also unconnected (N/C).
  #                    PMU software: load MaxxECU.canx template to map CAN channels.
  ECU_CMC:
    type: "Molex CMC 48-pin (MaxxECU Race / V1 / PRO)"
    subtype: "Source: maxxecu.com/webhelp/wirings-maxxecu_pinout.html"
    pincount: 48
    pinlabels:
      - "A1: GPO 5 (Rev light relay — Ph3 reassignment; ICV B freed)" # 1
      - "A2: IGN 1"                      # 2
      - "A3: IGN 2"                      # 3
      - "A4: GPO 8 / TACHO"             # 4
      - "B1: GPO 6 (FAN — CAN cmd → PMU16 O3)"  # 5
      - "B2: IGN 3"                      # 6
      - "B3: IGN 4"                      # 7
      - "B4: GPO 1 (Boost)"             # 8
      - "C1: GPO 7 / DIN3 (Flex)"       # 9
      - "C2: IGN 5"                      # 10
      - "C3: IGN 6 (unused 07K)"        # 11
      - "C4: GPO 2 (Fuel pump — CAN cmd → PMU16 O4)"  # 12
      - "D1: WBO2 Heater-"              # 13
      - "D2: IGN 7 (unused)"            # 14
      - "D3: IGN 8 (unused)"            # 15
      - "D4: GPO 3 (VVT actuator)"       # 16  — was VANOS; now 07K intake VVT solenoid
      - "E1: CAN H"                      # 17
      - "E2: CAN L"                      # 18
      - "E3: GND Shield"                # 19
      - "E4: GPO 4 (SPARE)"            # 20  — freed from ICV A; NOT ETh Motor-
      - "F1: CLT"                        # 21
      - "F2: IAT"                        # 22
      - "F3: WBO2 VREF"                  # 23
      - "F4: WBO2 VS"                    # 24
      - "G1: +5V sensor supply"         # 25
      - "G2: TPS1 / AIN (DBW TB)"       # 26  — M52 TPS → 07K DBW TPS1
      - "G3: WBO2 IP"                    # 27
      - "G4: WBO2 RCAL"                  # 28
      - "H1: Sensor GND"                # 29
      - "H2: Trigger GND (VR-)"        # 30
      - "H3: TRIGGER (crank VR+)"      # 31
      - "H4: HOME (cam Hall)"           # 32
      - "J1: AIN 1 (PST-F1 temp)"      # 33
      - "J2: AIN 2 (DBW TPS2)"         # 34  — was spare; 07K DBW TPS2
      - "J3: AIN 3 (PST-F1 pres)"      # 35
      - "J4: AIN 4 (MAP)"              # 36
      - "K1: INJ 1"                      # 37
      - "K2: INJ 2"                      # 38
      - "K3: DIN/VR 1 (Knock 1)"        # 39  — 07K: knock sensor 1
      - "K4: DIN/VR 2 (Knock 2)"        # 40  — 07K: knock sensor 2
      - "L1: INJ 8 (unused)"            # 41
      - "L2: INJ 7 (unused 07K)"        # 42
      - "L3: INJ 6 (unused 07K)"        # 43
      - "L4: Engine GND"                # 44
      - "M1: INJ 3"                      # 45
      - "M2: INJ 4"                      # 46
      - "M3: INJ 5"                      # 47
      - "M4: +12V ECU power"            # 48

  # ── MaxxECU C2 (32-pin Molex CMC) — clutch position + ETh motor outputs ────────
  ECU_C2:
    type: "Molex CMC 32-pin (MaxxECU Race C2)"
    subtype: "AIN 5 (clutch) + MOTOR 1+/1- (ETh) + AIN 6/7 (APS, cabin-side only)"
    pincount: 5
    pinlabels:
      - "G3: AIN 5 — clutch position signal (0-5V)"
      - "+5V sensor supply (C2 shared rail)"
      - "Sensor GND (C2 shared rail)"
      - "H4: MOTOR 1+ — ETh Motor+ → AS79 pin 22 → TB motor"
      - "H2: MOTOR 1- — ETh Motor- → AS79 pin 23 → TB motor"
    notes: >-
      C2 H4 (MOTOR 1+) and C2 H2 (MOTOR 1-) are the dedicated H-bridge outputs for
      the 07K DBW throttle body. NOT GPO3/4. These wires cross the AS79 bulkhead via
      cabin pins 22 and 23 respectively.
      AIN 6 (C2 E4) and AIN 7 (C2 F1) are used for APS1/APS2 from the E46 pedal --
      those are cabin-to-cabin wires and do not appear in engine-side connections here.
      Source: MaxxECU RACE GEN1 C2 pinout (maxxecu.com/webhelp/wirings-maxxecu_pinout.html).
      See maxxecu-m52.wv ECU_C2 for AIN 5 clutch wiring detail.

  # ── Virtual clutch pedal position sensor ─────────────────────────────────────
  # Identical to M52 harness — cabin-side, no re-work at engine swap.
  CLUTCH_POS_SENSOR:
    type: "Rotary position sensor 0-5V — E36 clutch pedal pivot"
    subtype: "Carries from Phase 1 M52 unchanged. Same pedal, same sensor, same C2 AIN 5."
    pincount: 3
    pinlabels: ["+5V", Signal, GND]
    notes: "No re-work required at 07K swap. See maxxecu-m52.wv CLUTCH_POS_SENSOR for full notes."

  # ── Cabin-side connectors — unchanged from M52, included to resolve diagram ──────

  DCT_SHIFTER:
    type: "DCT Shifter mechanical sequential"
    subtype: "DCT Shifter E36 (3-wire, no +12V supply needed)"
    pincount: 3
    pinlabels: ["UP (Black)", "DOWN (Blue)", "GND (Brown)"]
    notes: >
      Source: dctshifter.com/pages/installation — 3-wire only (no +12V).
      UP (Black) :: MaxxECU DIN 2 (Transmission UP shift).
      DOWN (Blue) :: MaxxECU DIN 1 (Transmission DOWN shift).
      GND (Brown) :: Sensor GND or chassis GND.
      MTune: Advanced :: 8HP :: Shifter type :: 8HP SEQ shifter.
      Cabin-to-cabin; does NOT cross firewall bulkhead. Unchanged from M52 phase.

  CAN_BUS_JUNCTION:
    type: "Splice / junction"
    subtype: "CAN H/L shared bus junction"
    pincount: 4
    pinlabels: ["CAN H in (ECU)", "CAN L in (ECU)", "CAN H out (8HP+GaugeS)", "CAN L out (8HP+GaugeS)"]
    notes: >
      MaxxECU CAN 1 (16-pin pins 9-10) feeds both the 8HP CAN harness and Gauge.S cluster.
      Bus speed: 500kbps. MaxxECU CAN 1 has built-in 120ohm terminator.
      Add 120ohm terminator at far end of bus if bus run over 1 meter total.

  HP8_CAN:
    type: "MaxxECU 8HP GEN1 CAN harness"
    subtype: "ZF 8HP70 transmission CAN connector"
    pincount: 2
    pinlabels: ["CAN H", "CAN L"]
    notes: "See harnesses/8hp-can.wv for full CAN + power wiring. Unchanged from M52 phase."

  GAUGES_CAN:
    type: "Gauge.S cluster CAN"
    subtype: "Gauge.S E36 PNP cluster CAN input"
    pincount: 2
    pinlabels: ["CAN H", "CAN L"]
    notes: >
      Gauge.S receives MaxxECU Default 1.3 CAN output (500kbps).
      Enable in MTune: CAN :: Default CAN output :: MaxxECU Default 1.3.
      Unchanged from M52 phase.

  # ── Engine-side mating plug (07K — replaces M52 mating plug at bulkhead) ────

  # ── Firewall bulkhead engine-side plug (07K Phase 3) — PIN REFERENCE ───────────
  # Connector type: Deutsch AS79 / Souriau 8STA 79-way jam nut plug (engine side)
  # Operation: Unplug M52 engine mating plug, insert 07K mating plug. Cabin side unchanged.
  # Full connector modeled in harnesses/firewall-bulkhead.wv (BULKHEAD_ENGINE_M52 / 07K notes).
  # Excluded from WireViz connectors here — bulkhead treated as transparent in this diagram.
  #
  # ── Confirmed AS79 pin assignments (cross-reference firewall-bulkhead.wv BULKHEAD_CABIN) ──
  #   Power rails (Option B — via bulkhead; Option A routes separately through DT grommet):
  #     1, 2, 29, 30: +12V Coils/Inj rails (four contacts in parallel, 4×5A = 20A)
  #     3, 31, 52:    Engine GND (three contacts in parallel, 3×5A = 15A)
  #   Ignition outputs (22 AWG max per size-22D contact):
  #     4: IGN 1 (CMC A2)   5: IGN 2 (CMC A3)   6: IGN 3 (CMC B2)   7: IGN 4 (CMC B3)
  #     32: IGN 5 (CMC C2)  33: IGN 6 [M52 only, cavity-plug 07K]    34: EXP IGN 7
  #   Injector outputs (22 AWG main harness through size-22D contact; pigtail stub engine-side can be 20 AWG after splice):
  #     8: INJ 1 (CMC K1)   9: INJ 2 (CMC K2)   10: INJ 3 (CMC M1)
  #     11: INJ 4 (CMC M2)  12: INJ 5 (CMC M3)  13: INJ 6 [M52 only, cavity-plug 07K]
  #   Crank / Cam triggers:
  #     16: Crank VR+ (CMC H3)  17: Crank VR- (CMC H2)  18: Crank shield drain
  #     19: Cam Hall signal (CMC H4)   [M52 + 07K — same pins, swap connector body only]
  #   DBW throttle body (07K only; cavity-plug on M52):
  #     22: ETh Motor+ → MaxxECU C2 H4 (MOTOR 1+)   23: ETh Motor- → MaxxECU C2 H2 (MOTOR 1-)
  #     48: TPS1 (CMC G2)   56: TPS2 / AIN 2 (CMC J2)   [+5V from 47, GND from 79]
  #   Sensor signals:
  #     25: CLT (CMC F1)   26: IAT (CMC F2)   27: Flex fuel +12V
  #     47: +5V sensor supply (CMC G1 — TPS/MAP/PST-F1/Cam/07K DBW TPS)
  #     48: TPS1 signal (CMC G2)   49: MAP signal (AIN 4)   79: Sensor GND (CMC H1, center pin)
  #   GPO actuators:
  #     35: GPO 3 → VANOS (M52) / VVT solenoid (07K)   36: GPO 4 → ICV-A (M52) / SPARE (07K)
  #     37: GPO 5 → ICV-B (M52) / Rev light relay (07K — MTune reassignment, no rewiring)   38: Starter trigger   39: Alt D+
  #   Knock sensors (07K only; cavity-plug on M52):
  #     43: Knock 1 signal (CMC K3)   44: Knock 2 signal (CMC K4)   45: Knock GND / shield drain
  #   Misc:
  #     64: Flex fuel signal (CMC C1 / DIN3)
  #   Pins 20, 24, 41, 50–63, 65–78: SPARE / cavity-plug
  #   Pins 72–79 (except 79): SPARE — APS is cabin-to-cabin, no bulkhead crossing needed

  # ── 07K engine sensors / actuators ─────────────────────────────────────────

  CRANK_VR:
    type: "VW 07K crank VR sensor connector"
    subtype: "60-2 missing tooth passive VR — MaxxECU VR input (N-1 trigger type)"
    pincount: 3
    pinlabels: [Signal+, Signal-, Shield]
    notes: >
      OE# 3B0973703G — same connector body as CAM_HALL but DIFFERENT pinout.
      Crank: Signal+/Signal-/Shield (passive VR). Cam: +5V/GND/Signal (active Hall).
      LABEL PIGTAILS AT CRIMP TIME — swapped pigtails produce no-start with no
      obvious failure indicator. MTune: VR input, trigger N-1 / 60-2 pattern, same
      type as M52 crank. Only crank angle offset may differ — confirm in MTune
      Trigger Setup before first crank. ME7.1.1 harness ref: Conn B pin 82.
      Location: cylinder 5 side — sensor G28 "secured to the control housing cover"
      (timing chain compartment cover at cylinder 5 end).
      Source: charm.li CBTA/BGP component locations, item 12.

  CAM_HALL:
    type: "VW 07K cam Hall sensor connector"
    subtype: "Hall effect, intake side top of head — +5V supply type (not +12V)"
    pincount: 3
    pinlabels: ["+5V", "Sensor GND", Signal]
    notes: >
      TODO: Confirm exact VW connector body type at install.
      ME7.1.1 harness ref: pin 86. +5V supply shared with MAP/TPS/PST-F1 (bulkhead pin 47).
      Signal → HOME input (CMC H4 = pin 32). Same bulkhead pin 25 as M52 cam.

  CLT:
    type: "VW 07K coolant temp sensor 2-pin"
    subtype: "NTC thermistor — cylinder 1 side, exhaust face of block"
    pincount: 2
    pinlabels: [Signal, "Sensor GND"]
    notes: >
      ME7.1.1 ref: pin 93. TODO: verify VW-specific 2-pin connector housing at engine.
      BGP source: the07k.wiki/upload/f/fd/BGP_Wiring_diagram.pdf (Diagram 4, "right rear").
      Location: cylinder 1 side + exhaust side. In E36: front of engine, exhaust face.
      Route pigtail with heat sleeving (exhaust manifold adjacent).

  IAT:
    type: "VW 07K intake air temp sensor 2-pin"
    subtype: "NTC thermistor — airbox or intake pipe"
    pincount: 2
    pinlabels: [Signal, "Sensor GND"]
    notes: "Mount in intake pipe downstream of intercooler. TODO: confirm connector body at install."

  MAP:
    type: "Bosch MAP sensor 3-pin"
    subtype: "3-bar for turbo application (GM 12592525 or equivalent)"
    pincount: 3
    pinlabels: ["+5V", Signal, GND]
    notes: >
      Same sensor as M52 phase, upgrade to 3-bar if still on stock 1-bar.
      Route vacuum hose to BBG intake manifold (post-throttle body) for boost-corrected MAP.

  DBW_TB:
    type: "VW 07K DBW throttle body 6-pin"
    subtype: "Stock ~65mm bore. Upgrade to VR6 03H133062 74mm for 600+ whp."
    pincount: 6
    pinlabels:
      - "TPS1 signal (0-5V)"  # 1
      - "TPS2 signal (0-5V)"  # 2
      - "+5V sensor supply"   # 3
      - "Sensor GND"          # 4
      - "Motor+"              # 5
      - "Motor-"              # 6
    notes: >
      TODO: Confirm VW TB connector body and motor wire polarity at install.
      ME7.1.1 ref: Motor+=pin84, Motor-=pin92, TPS1=pin117, TPS2=pin118.
      MaxxECU ETh1 motor: C2 H4 (MOTOR 1+) → AS79 pin 22 → TB Motor+.
                           C2 H2 (MOTOR 1-) → AS79 pin 23 → TB Motor-.
      NOT GPO3/GPO4. C2 MOTOR 1+/1- are the correct H-bridge outputs.
      Source: MaxxECU RACE GEN1 C2 pinout (maxxecu.com/webhelp/wirings-maxxecu_pinout.html).
      MTune: Settings → E-Throttle → Motor output → Motor 1.
      IMPORTANT: verify motor polarity with volt meter before wiring — swap Motor+/-
      at TB connector if throttle runs in wrong direction during e-throttle wizard.
      TPS1 → CMC G2 (pin 26) / AS79 pin 48 (was M52 TPS — same wire).
      TPS2 → CMC J2 (AIN 2, pin 34) / AS79 pin 56 (was ATF temp spare — repurposed).
      +5V → AS79 pin 47 (shared +5V rail, CMC G1). GND → AS79 pin 79 (SGND, CMC H1).
      Calibrate in MTune :: Throttle :: E-Throttle wizard.

  KNOCK_1:
    type: "Bosch flat knock sensor 1-pin (M8 bolt mount)"
    subtype: "Exhaust side, lower block — 07K block"
    pincount: 1
    pinlabels: ["KS1 signal"]
    notes: >
      GND via M8 mounting bolt to block — no separate GND wire.
      ME7.1.1 ref: pin 106. MaxxECU: CMC K3 (DIN/VR1, pin 39).
      AS79 bulkhead: signal via pin 43 (EXP: Knock sensor 1). Shield drain via pin 45.
      Location: "back side of engine block" = exhaust side (both KS1 and KS2).
      Source: charm.li CBTA/BGP component locations — "Knock Sensors" section.

  KNOCK_2:
    type: "Bosch flat knock sensor 1-pin (M8 bolt mount)"
    subtype: "Exhaust side, lower block — 07K block"
    pincount: 1
    pinlabels: ["KS2 signal"]
    notes: >
      GND via M8 mounting bolt. ME7.1.1 ref: pin 107.
      MaxxECU: CMC K4 (DIN/VR2, pin 40). AS79 bulkhead: signal via pin 44. Shield drain via pin 45.

  # ── Ignition (5-cyl — same VAG 4-way COP as M52; S54 COPs retained) ─────────

  IGN_1:
    type: "VAG 4-way COP"
    subtype: "Coil 1 — cyl 1 (07K firing order: 1-2-4-5-3)"
    pincount: 4
    pinlabels: ["+12V", GND, Signal, Shield]

  IGN_2:
    type: "VAG 4-way COP"
    subtype: "Coil 2 — cyl 2"
    pincount: 4
    pinlabels: ["+12V", GND, Signal, Shield]

  IGN_3:
    type: "VAG 4-way COP"
    subtype: "Coil 3 — cyl 3"
    pincount: 4
    pinlabels: ["+12V", GND, Signal, Shield]

  IGN_4:
    type: "VAG 4-way COP"
    subtype: "Coil 4 — cyl 4"
    pincount: 4
    pinlabels: ["+12V", GND, Signal, Shield]

  IGN_5:
    type: "VAG 4-way COP"
    subtype: "Coil 5 — cyl 5"
    pincount: 4
    pinlabels: ["+12V", GND, Signal, Shield]

  # ── Fuel injectors (EV14; M50 harness has EV1 pigtails — swap at build) ────

  INJ_1:
    type: "Bosch EV14 2-pin (USCAR)"
    subtype: "Injector 1 (ID1050x)"
    pincount: 2
    pinlabels: ["+12V", "INJ 1"]
    notes: >-
      MaxxECU M50 harness ships with EV1 connector ends — replace with EV14 pigtails for 07K.
      Product: http://injectordynamics.com/injectors/id1050-xds/

  INJ_2:
    type: "Bosch EV14 2-pin (USCAR)"
    subtype: "Injector 2 (ID1050x)"
    pincount: 2
    pinlabels: ["+12V", "INJ 2"]

  INJ_3:
    type: "Bosch EV14 2-pin (USCAR)"
    subtype: "Injector 3 (ID1050x)"
    pincount: 2
    pinlabels: ["+12V", "INJ 3"]

  INJ_4:
    type: "Bosch EV14 2-pin (USCAR)"
    subtype: "Injector 4 (ID1050x)"
    pincount: 2
    pinlabels: ["+12V", "INJ 4"]

  INJ_5:
    type: "Bosch EV14 2-pin (USCAR)"
    subtype: "Injector 5 (ID1050x)"
    pincount: 2
    pinlabels: ["+12V", "INJ 5"]

  # ── Shared / unchanged sensors ────────────────────────────────────────────────

  PST_F1:
    type: "Bosch PST-F1 4-pin"
    subtype: "Dual oil temp+pressure — iABED M10x1.0 port on 07K oil housing"
    pincount: 4
    pinlabels: ["+5V", GND, "Pressure (0-5V)", "Temp (NTC)"]
    notes: >
      Same wiring as M52 phase — zero connector or cable changes.
      Mount: iABED 07K longitudinal oil housing M10x1.0 built-in port.
      Pressure → AIN 3 (0-5V, 0-10 bar). Temp → AIN 1 (NTC).

  WIDEBAND:
    type: "Bosch LSU 4.9 6-way"
    subtype: "Wideband lambda sensor"
    pincount: 6
    pinlabels: ["IP", "VREF", "H-", "H+", "RCAL", "VS"]
    notes: >
      Same ECU-side cable structure as M52 (same 5-wire cable, same CMC channels).
      Sensor-side pin numbers differ from LSU 4.2 — use pinlabels above, not M52 diagram.
      Bung: weld 18mm x1.5 in 07K custom top-mount exhaust manifold, min 6in from collector, upstream of turbo.
      Sensor: Bosch 0 258 017 025 (LSU 4.9).
      Product: https://www.bosch-motorsport.com/products/sensors/lambda/lambda-sensor-lsu-4-9/
      Pin numbering source: maxxecu.com/webhelp/wirings-lambda_sensors.html (LSU 4.9 table).
      Wire colors: red=IP(1), yellow=VREF(2), white=H-(3), grey=H+(4), green=RCAL(5), black=VS(6).
      Always verify by wire color — do not rely on pin number alone.

  VVT_SOL:
    type: "VW/Tyco Micro Timer 1.5mm Sealed — 2-pin (1J0 973 802 male on solenoid)"
    subtype: "N205 camshaft adjustment valve. OEM solenoid: 06E 109 257 P. MaxxECU GPO 3 (CMC D4 = pin 16)."
    pincount: 2
    pinlabels: ["+12V", "GPO 3 (low-side)"]
    notes: >
      07K intake cam VVT actuator solenoid (N205 — camshaft adjustment valve 1).
      Solenoid OEM PN: 06E 109 257 P (covers 06E109257F/J/AA). Resistance: 5–9 Ω at 20°C.
      Connector series: VW/Tyco "Micro Timer" 1.5mm Sealed.
        Solenoid side (male): 1J0 973 802 (FEP 42062500 / TE 1-966701-1).
        Harness side (female pigtail): 1J0 973 702 (FEP 42121600 / TE 1-969850-1).
        Pre-made pigtail: automotive-connectors.com 42121600-PT (~30 cm leads)
                          or Amazon B0D8FH4S8T (~170 mm leads, fits Jetta 2.5L).
        Terminals: 0.35–0.5 mm² → VW N 10335706 / Tyco 969019-2; 0.5–1.0 mm² → N 10335807 / Tyco 964275-2.
        Wire size: 22 AWG (0.35 mm²) adequate for solenoid drive current.
      Pin 1 (+12V): switched +12V from coil/inj relay (ECU_12PIN[1]).
      Pin 2 (control): MaxxECU GPO 3 (CMC D4/pin 16) — LOW-SIDE switch (ECM grounds pin 2 to actuate).
        MTune: Settings → Outputs → GPO 3 → Output type: Negative (low-side) → Function: PWM Solenoid
               → assign to Cam VVT control. Duty cycle 0% = cam retarded; higher DC = more advance.
               Max advance: ~42° crank degrees. PWM frequency: 100–200 Hz.
      AS79 bulkhead: GPO 3 signal crosses via CABIN pin 35 (engine-side 07K plug pin 35).
      Flyback diode: 1N4007 at solenoid connector, cathode (banded end) to +12V pin (1), anode to GPO pin (2).
      Source: VW BGP/BGQ workshop manual (solenoid resistance, pin function);
              automotivetechinfo.com 2010 Golf valve timing repair (connector PN confirmation);
              automotive-connectors.com (pigtail PN).

  BOOST_SOL:
    type: "Superseal 2-way"
    subtype: "Turbosmart boost solenoid (2-port PWM)"
    pincount: 2
    pinlabels: ["+12V", "GPO 1 signal"]
    notes: >
      Same wiring as M52. GPO 1 (CMC B4/pin 8). +12V from coil/inj relay (ECU_12PIN[1]).
      Flyback diode: 1N4007 at connector, cathode (banded end) to +12V pin, anode to GPO 1 pin.

  FLEX_FUEL:
    type: "Continental 3-pin (GM 13577429)"
    subtype: "Flex fuel composition sensor — retain from M52, unchanged"
    pincount: 3
    pinlabels: ["+12V", GND, "Signal (PWM out)"]
    notes: >
      GM 13577429 / Continental SE1004S. Pin A=+12V (system voltage — NOT 5V), Pin B=GND, Pin C=signal.
      Signal encodes ethanol % (frequency) and fuel temperature (pulse width) on one wire.
      Inline on fuel feed — position unchanged from M52. Zero wiring changes at Phase 3.
      +12V from coil/inj relay (ECU_12PIN[1]) — see connection block for correct routing.


cables:

  # ── Crank / Cam ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  W_CRANK:
    wirecount: 3
    colors: [WH, BK, GY]
    wirelabels: [Signal+, Signal-, Shield]
    length: 1.0 m
    notes: "Shielded twisted pair. Shield terminates at CMC E3 (GND Shield, pin 19) — dedicated shield ground, not sensor GND bus."

  W_CAM:
    wirecount: 3
    colors: [RD, BK, WH]
    wirelabels: ["+5V", "Sensor GND", Signal]
    length: 0.8 m
    shield: true
    notes: >-
      +5V from shared sensor rail (CMC G1/pin 25 → AS79 pin 47).
      Shielded recommended — cam Hall signal runs in Sector 1 near crank trigger and coil primaries.
      Shield drain terminates at CMC E3 (GND Shield, pin 19). Float at sensor side.

  # ── Temperature / pressure sensors ────────────────────────────────────────────
  W_CLT:
    wirecount: 2
    colors: [WH, BK]
    wirelabels: [Signal, GND]
    length: 0.5 m

  W_IAT:
    wirecount: 2
    colors: [WH, BK]
    wirelabels: [Signal, GND]
    length: 0.5 m

  W_MAP:
    wirecount: 3
    colors: [RD, WH, BK]
    wirelabels: ["+5V", Signal, GND]
    length: 0.5 m

  W_PST_F1:
    wirecount: 4
    colors: [RD, BK, GN, YE]
    wirelabels: ["+5V", GND, "Pressure (AIN 3)", "Temp (AIN 1)"]
    length: 0.6 m
    notes: "Same cable as M52 build — no change."

  # ── DBW throttle body ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  W_DBW_TPS:
    wirecount: 4
    colors: [RD, BK, WH, GN]
    wirelabels: ["+5V", GND, "TPS1 signal", "TPS2 signal"]
    length: 0.5 m

  W_DBW_MOTOR:
    wirecount: 2
    colors: [OG, VT]
    wirelabels: ["Motor+ (C2 H4 MOTOR 1+)", "Motor- (C2 H2 MOTOR 1-)"]
    length: 0.5 m
    notes: >-
      22 AWG (size-22D contact accepts 22–26 AWG only; 3A peak, 0.5 m — 22 AWG adequate). Verify polarity at TB before final crimp.
      Engine-side wires terminate at throttle body motor leads (OE ref: pin 84 Mot+, pin 92 Mot-).
      Cabin side of this wire goes to MaxxECU C2 H4/H2 via AS79 pins 22/23.

  # ── Knock sensors ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  W_KNOCK_1:
    wirecount: 2
    colors: [WH, GY]
    wirelabels: ["KS1 signal", "Shield drain"]
    length: 0.4 m
    shield: true
    notes: >-
      GND via M8 mounting bolt — no GND wire.
      Shield drain (wire 2) terminates at CMC H1 (Sensor GND, pin 29) via AS79 pin 45.
      Float at sensor side. Per firewall-bulkhead.wv knock note.
      ROUTING: Both KS1/KS2 sensors are on the exhaust side of the block.
      Route pigtails down the block face, away from the exhaust manifold, then
      bundle into KNOCK sub-loom across the bottom of the engine.
      If any section runs within 100 mm (4 in) of exhaust manifold, wrap with
      DEI Reflect-A-Gold (p/n 010394, 1-1/2"x15' roll, $42.99 — designengineering.com/reflect-a-gold-heat-reflective-tape-1-5-x-15/)
      over the Techflex sleeve before tie-strapping. Reflect-A-Gold is a metalized
      polyimide laminated glass cloth, 800°F continuous (adhesive rated 325°F).
      NOT to be confused with Reflect-A-Cool (fiberglass foil sheet, 400°F).

  W_KNOCK_2:
    wirecount: 2
    colors: [WH, GY]
    wirelabels: ["KS2 signal", "Shield drain"]
    length: 0.4 m
    shield: true
    notes: >-
      Shield drain terminates at CMC H1 (Sensor GND, pin 29) via AS79 pin 45 (shared with KS1).
      See W_KNOCK_1 for routing and heat management spec.

  # ── Ignition coils (5-cyl) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  W_IGN_1:
    wirecount: 4
    colors: [RD, BK, WH, GY]
    wirelabels: ["+12V", GND, Signal, Shield]
    length: 0.5 m

  W_IGN_2:
    wirecount: 4
    colors: [RD, BK, WH, GY]
    wirelabels: ["+12V", GND, Signal, Shield]
    length: 0.5 m

  W_IGN_3:
    wirecount: 4
    colors: [RD, BK, WH, GY]
    wirelabels: ["+12V", GND, Signal, Shield]
    length: 0.5 m

  W_IGN_4:
    wirecount: 4
    colors: [RD, BK, WH, GY]
    wirelabels: ["+12V", GND, Signal, Shield]
    length: 0.5 m

  W_IGN_5:
    wirecount: 4
    colors: [RD, BK, WH, GY]
    wirelabels: ["+12V", GND, Signal, Shield]
    length: 0.5 m

  # ── Injectors (EV14; 5-cyl) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  W_INJ_1:
    wirecount: 2
    colors: [RD, GN]
    wirelabels: ["+12V", "INJ 1"]
    length: 0.4 m

  W_INJ_2:
    wirecount: 2
    colors: [RD, GN]
    wirelabels: ["+12V", "INJ 2"]
    length: 0.4 m

  W_INJ_3:
    wirecount: 2
    colors: [RD, GN]
    wirelabels: ["+12V", "INJ 3"]
    length: 0.4 m

  W_INJ_4:
    wirecount: 2
    colors: [RD, GN]
    wirelabels: ["+12V", "INJ 4"]
    length: 0.4 m

  W_INJ_5:
    wirecount: 2
    colors: [RD, GN]
    wirelabels: ["+12V", "INJ 5"]
    length: 0.4 m

  # Virtual clutch position sensor — cabin-side, carries unchanged from M52
  W_CLUTCH_POS:
    wirecount: 3
    colors: [RD, WH, BK]
    wirelabels: ["+5V", "AIN 5 signal", GND]
    length: 0.8 m
    notes: "Unchanged from M52 phase. See maxxecu-m52.wv W_CLUTCH_POS for full notes."

  # ── Cabin-side cables — unchanged from M52 ────────────────────────────────────

  W_CAN:
    wirecount: 2
    colors: [WH, BU]
    wirelabels: ["CAN H", "CAN L"]
    length: 2.0 m
    notes: "Twisted pair. 120ohm at far end if bus run over 1 m. Unchanged from M52 phase."

  W_SHIFTER:
    wirecount: 3
    colors: [BK, BU, BN]
    wirelabels: ["UP (DIN 2)", "DOWN (DIN 1)", GND]
    length: 1.5 m
    notes: "DCT Shifter paddle harness. Unchanged from M52 phase."

  W_FLEXFUEL:
    wirecount: 3
    colors: [RD, BK, WH]
    wirelabels: ["+12V", GND, "Signal (DIN 3)"]
    length: 0.8 m
    notes: "Retain flex fuel sensor if present. Unchanged from M52 phase."

  W_CAN_8HP:
    wirecount: 2
    colors: [WH, BU]
    wirelabels: ["CAN H", "CAN L"]
    length: 0.3 m
    notes: "CAN junction → 8HP GEN1 harness. Unchanged from M52 phase."

  W_CAN_GAUGES:
    wirecount: 2
    colors: [WH, BU]
    wirelabels: ["CAN H", "CAN L"]
    length: 0.3 m
    notes: "CAN junction → Gauge.S cluster. Unchanged from M52 phase."

  # ── Wideband / Boost ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  W_WBO2:
    wirecount: 5
    colors: [WH, WH, WH, WH, BK]
    wirelabels: ["WBO2 VS", "WBO2 VREF", "WBO2 IP", "WBO2 RCAL", "WBO2 Htr-"]
    length: 1.5 m
    shield: true
    notes: >-
      Same wiring as M52. Heater+ (LSU 4.9 pin 4 / H+) splices to local +12V coil rail — see W_WBO2_HTR.
      Shielded — VS/VREF/IP/RCAL are low-level analog signals susceptible to
      injector/coil noise. Single-end drain at ECU end only.
      HEAT MANAGEMENT: Bung is on the custom top-mount exhaust manifold. Sleeve the
      first 300 mm (12 in) from the sensor body with DEI Fire Sleeve 3/8" ID
      (p/n 010470, 3/8"x36" kit, $26.99 — designengineering.com/fire-sleeve-tape-kit-0-375-id-x-36/;
      silicone-over-fiberglass, 500°F/260°C continuous, 2000°F intermittent). Transition
      to Techflex F6 after clearing the manifold/turbo heat zone.
      Route away from turbo turbine housing and wastegate — minimum 100 mm clearance.
      Tie-strap cable to manifold stud boss or block surface to prevent contact with
      hot metal under vibration.

  W_VVT_SOL:
    wirecount: 2
    colors: [RD, GN]
    wirelabels: ["+12V", "GPO 3 (VVT)"]
    length: 0.6 m
    notes: "22 AWG (size-22D contact; 22 AWG adequate for solenoid drive current). Flyback diode at solenoid connector. Route in actuators sub-loom with boost solenoid."

  W_WBO2_HTR:
    wirecount: 1
    colors: [RD]
    wirelabels: ["WBO2 Hs+ (heater+)"]
    length: 0.3 m
    notes: "Splices to +12V coil/inj rail on engine side (ECU_12PIN[1]). Short stub — splice at rail, no ECU termination."

  W_BOOST:
    wirecount: 2
    colors: [RD, GN]
    wirelabels: ["+12V", "GPO 1"]
    length: 0.5 m


connections:

  # ── Crank trigger ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  # TRIGGER+ = H3/CMC pin 31, TRIGGER- = H2/CMC pin 30, Shield = E3/CMC pin 19
  - - CRANK_VR: [1, 2, 3]
    - W_CRANK: [1, 2, 3]
    - ECU_CMC: [31, 30, 19]

  # ── Cam / HOME trigger ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  # Signal = H4/CMC pin 32, GND = H1/CMC pin 29, +5V = G1/CMC pin 25
  - - CAM_HALL: [3, 2, 1]
    - W_CAM: [3, 2, 1]
    - ECU_CMC: [32, 29, 25]

  # ── CLT ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - - CLT: [1, 2]
    - W_CLT: [1, 2]
    - ECU_CMC: [21, 29]

  # ── IAT ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - - IAT: [1, 2]
    - W_IAT: [1, 2]
    - ECU_CMC: [22, 29]

  # ── MAP ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - - MAP: [1, 2, 3]
    - W_MAP: [1, 2, 3]
    - ECU_CMC: [25, 36, 29]

  # ── DBW throttle body — TPS signals ──────────────────────────────────────────
  # TPS1 signal = G2/CMC pin 26 (was M52 cable TPS); TPS2 = J2/CMC pin 34
  - - DBW_TB: [3, 4, 1, 2]
    - W_DBW_TPS: [1, 2, 3, 4]
    - ECU_CMC: [25, 29, 26, 34]

  # ── DBW throttle body — motor (C2 H4/H2 internal H-bridge) ─────────────────────
  # Motor+ = C2 H4 (MOTOR 1+) → AS79 pin 22; Motor- = C2 H2 (MOTOR 1-) → AS79 pin 23
  - - DBW_TB: [5, 6]
    - W_DBW_MOTOR: [1, 2]
    - ECU_C2: [4, 5]

  # ── Knock sensors (via AS79 pins 43/44/45 → CMC K3/K4; GND via M8 bolt to block) ──
  # Shield drain for both sensors shares AS79 pin 45 → CMC H1 (Sensor GND, pin 29)
  - - KNOCK_1: [1]
    - W_KNOCK_1: [1]
    - ECU_CMC: [39]

  - - W_KNOCK_1: [2]
    - ECU_CMC: [29]

  - - KNOCK_2: [1]
    - W_KNOCK_2: [1]
    - ECU_CMC: [40]

  - - W_KNOCK_2: [2]
    - ECU_CMC: [29]

  # ── Ignition coils ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  # +12V from coil/inj relay (ECU_12PIN[1]) — NOT ECU_CMC[48] (ECU logic power).
  # GND=L4/CMC44, Shield=E3/CMC19
  # Firing order: 1-2-4-5-3 → IGN 1-5 = CMC pins 2/3/6/7/10
  - - IGN_1: [1]
    - W_IGN_1: [1]
    - ECU_12PIN: [1]

  - - IGN_1: [2, 3, 4]
    - W_IGN_1: [2, 3, 4]
    - ECU_CMC: [44, 2, 19]

  - - IGN_2: [1]
    - W_IGN_2: [1]
    - ECU_12PIN: [1]

  - - IGN_2: [2, 3, 4]
    - W_IGN_2: [2, 3, 4]
    - ECU_CMC: [44, 3, 19]

  - - IGN_3: [1]
    - W_IGN_3: [1]
    - ECU_12PIN: [1]

  - - IGN_3: [2, 3, 4]
    - W_IGN_3: [2, 3, 4]
    - ECU_CMC: [44, 6, 19]

  - - IGN_4: [1]
    - W_IGN_4: [1]
    - ECU_12PIN: [1]

  - - IGN_4: [2, 3, 4]
    - W_IGN_4: [2, 3, 4]
    - ECU_CMC: [44, 7, 19]

  - - IGN_5: [1]
    - W_IGN_5: [1]
    - ECU_12PIN: [1]

  - - IGN_5: [2, 3, 4]
    - W_IGN_5: [2, 3, 4]
    - ECU_CMC: [44, 10, 19]

  # ── Injectors ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  # +12V from coil/inj relay (ECU_12PIN[1]) — NOT ECU_CMC[48] (ECU logic power).
  # INJ signals = CMC K1/K2/M1/M2/M3 = pins 37/38/45/46/47
  - - INJ_1: [1]
    - W_INJ_1: [1]
    - ECU_12PIN: [1]

  - - INJ_1: [2]
    - W_INJ_1: [2]
    - ECU_CMC: [37]

  - - INJ_2: [1]
    - W_INJ_2: [1]
    - ECU_12PIN: [1]

  - - INJ_2: [2]
    - W_INJ_2: [2]
    - ECU_CMC: [38]

  - - INJ_3: [1]
    - W_INJ_3: [1]
    - ECU_12PIN: [1]

  - - INJ_3: [2]
    - W_INJ_3: [2]
    - ECU_CMC: [45]

  - - INJ_4: [1]
    - W_INJ_4: [1]
    - ECU_12PIN: [1]

  - - INJ_4: [2]
    - W_INJ_4: [2]
    - ECU_CMC: [46]

  - - INJ_5: [1]
    - W_INJ_5: [1]
    - ECU_12PIN: [1]

  - - INJ_5: [2]
    - W_INJ_5: [2]
    - ECU_CMC: [47]

  # ── PST-F1 oil sensor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - - PST_F1: [1, 2, 3, 4]
    - W_PST_F1: [1, 2, 3, 4]
    - ECU_CMC: [25, 29, 35, 33]

  # ── Wideband O2 (LSU 4.9) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  # Pin numbering per maxxecu.com/webhelp/wirings-lambda_sensors.html (LSU 4.9):
  # ECU inputs: VS(6)→F4[24], VREF(2)→F3[23], IP(1)→G3[27], RCAL(5)→G4[28], H-(3)→D1[13]
  # H+ (pin 4) splices to local +12V coil rail — separate connection below
  - - WIDEBAND: [6, 2, 1, 5, 3]
    - W_WBO2: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
    - ECU_CMC: [24, 23, 27, 28, 13]

  # WBO2 heater positive: WIDEBAND pin 4 (H+) → splice to +12V coil/inj rail
  - - WIDEBAND: [4]
    - W_WBO2_HTR: [1]
    - ECU_12PIN: [1]

  # ── VVT solenoid (07K intake cam) — GPO 3 ─────────────────────────────────────
  - - ECU_12PIN: [1]
    - W_VVT_SOL: [1]
    - VVT_SOL: [1]

  - - VVT_SOL: [2]
    - W_VVT_SOL: [2]
    - ECU_CMC: [16]

  # ── Boost solenoid ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - - ECU_12PIN: [1]
    - W_BOOST: [1]
    - BOOST_SOL: [1]

  - - BOOST_SOL: [2]
    - W_BOOST: [2]
    - ECU_CMC: [8]

  # ── Virtual clutch position sensor (cabin-side, unchanged from M52) ───────────
  # +5V=ECU_C2[2], Signal=ECU_C2[1] (AIN 5 / C2 pin G3), GND=ECU_C2[3]
  - - CLUTCH_POS_SENSOR: [1, 2, 3]
    - W_CLUTCH_POS: [1, 2, 3]
    - ECU_C2: [2, 1, 3]

  # ── CAN bus (shared: 8HP + Gauge.S) — unchanged from M52 ─────────────────────
  - - ECU_16PIN: [10, 9]
    - W_CAN: [1, 2]
    - CAN_BUS_JUNCTION: [1, 2]

  - - CAN_BUS_JUNCTION: [3, 4]
    - W_CAN_8HP: [1, 2]
    - HP8_CAN: [1, 2]

  - - CAN_BUS_JUNCTION: [3, 4]
    - W_CAN_GAUGES: [1, 2]
    - GAUGES_CAN: [1, 2]

  # ── DCT Shifter — cabin-to-cabin, unchanged from M52 ─────────────────────────
  # UP(BK)=DIN2=ECU_16PIN[15], DOWN(BU)=DIN1=ECU_16PIN[16], GND=ECU_16PIN[2]
  - - DCT_SHIFTER: [1, 2, 3]
    - W_SHIFTER: [1, 2, 3]
    - ECU_16PIN: [15, 16, 2]

  # ── Flex fuel sensor — unchanged from M52 ────────────────────────────────────
  # +12V from coil/inj relay (ECU_12PIN[1], 20A fused) — NOT ECU_16PIN[1] (+5V OUT).
  - - FLEX_FUEL: [1]
    - W_FLEXFUEL: [1]
    - ECU_12PIN: [1]

  - - FLEX_FUEL: [2, 3]
    - W_FLEXFUEL: [2, 3]
    - ECU_16PIN: [2, 5]
